analysisWe need to produce an assert statement for the comment inside removeLastOccurrence method.

Comment: "// @@@ If the element was in the deque before the operation, then the result is true."

Interpretation: The method returns boolean result. The spec: If the element was present in the deque before the operation, then the result (return value) is true. Conversely, if not present, result may be false (but not required). So we need to assert: (\old(this.contains(o))) => \result == true. Since contains method is public observer. Use this.contains(o). Use \old to capture pre-state.

Thus assert: \old(this.contains(o)) => \result; (since \result is boolean, true is equivalent). Could also write => \result == true. Use parentheses.

Thus final answer:

<code>assert \old(this.contains(o)) => \result;</code>

